1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
In a quiet village nestled between green hills, there lived an old man named Min.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Every morning before sunrise, Min would walk to the edge of town to tend a small garden.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:17,000
It wasn't flashy, just rows of vegetables and a few fruit trees, but it thrived.

4
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:23,000
Rain or shine, Min worked quietly, humming to himself, never boasting about his efforts.

5
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:27,000
Over time, his garden became the lifeline of the village.

6
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:31,000
During droughts, he shared water from a well he had dug himself.

7
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:36,000
During storms, he offered his harvest freely to those who lost their own crops.

8
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:42,000
People often asked him, why don't you open a market or take credit for what you do? You could be famous!

9
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Min would simply smile and say, the soil doesn't shout when it grows the tree, why should I?

10
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:53,000
Years passed. New farmers arrived with machines and loud claims.

11
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:57,000
But their crops often failed in the unpredictable weather.

12
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:03,000
When they asked Min for advice, he welcomed them without judgment, showing them his quiet methods.

13
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:07,000
Eventually, the village built a statue in Min's honor.

14
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:10,000
But true to his nature, Min never visited it.

15
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:19,000
He was busy planting new seeds, teaching children how to nurture life from the earth, without pride, without noise, only care.

16
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:27,000
And even when he passed on, the villagers remembered not just his garden, but the way he carried himself, with quiet strength, and a heart full of modesty.

